 "title": "Shared band table: centres, weights, faint thresholds, kernels, readability windows and gains",
 "description": "One table for every consumer of band readings (organic-evidence levels, ZooMS pattern, C1, close-ups). A reading r_b = mean of E over centre +- half_width_nm, E = scale x Savitzky-Golay derivative of absorbance (kernel 'e31'). u_b = r_b / weight. Band readability is ONE gate per band, shared by the evidence levels and the ZooMS pattern (so a close-up always matches the call): readable unless SD_E > 0.25 x weight and r_b < 1.5 x weight (thresholds owned by the rule files); SD_E from the band's readability block. A band with a 'projection' is read on that projection's corrected E (see 'projections'); u_b = u_sign x r_b / weight (u_sign -1: a trough, more collagen = more negative E; default +1).",
