 "provenance": {
  "weights_and_faint": "weights = median band ratios over the reference bones with >= 1% yield (public calibration data); faint thresholds = rounded 99th percentiles of collagen-free archaeological fauna (statistics only, unreleased collection, anonymised)",
  "gains": "detector-local correlated noise (white noise in absorbance smoothed by a 1.25 nm Gaussian) propagated exactly through the band kernel and the transfer (blur x detector gain), linearised; Monte Carlo through the engine agrees to 0.2%",
  "gate_reconciliation": "Phase 0b item 11. The gate's gains are the correlated-noise gains (0.017729 E per N2 standard; 0.008441 after v0.1), not white-noise values. The ~2x excess found by an earlier Monte Carlo is real non-stationary noise: on noisy high-res scans, N2 near 1689/1728 is 1.6-2.2x N2(1500-1600) and near 2262/2284 1.5-2.2x N2(2000-2100) (detector response falls toward the detector ends; a curvature-free high-pass estimate agrees). Scaling the SWIR1 C-H gates by that shape (x1.64 / x1.76) made the high-res evidence level agree LESS with the standard-res partner (kappa 0.78 -> 0.55; 2.5% more can't tell on the noisy session), so the gate keeps window N2 with the analytic gains: SD_E is a calibrated noise index, about half the true local SD at the far C-H bands on noisy high-res scans. Gains refreshed for transfer v0.2 (SWIR1 x 0.7050/0.6343, SWIR2 x 0.6258/0.6343)."
 },
